    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d866">

                <pb facs="1002" n="906" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg906"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">667.003/139: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-18T15:00:00+03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                                1921—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 19—6:13
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>232. Urgently request instructions concerning taxation plan set forth in my 221,
                    July 23, 12 a.m. [<hi rendition="#italic">July 24, noon</hi>]. Reports now
                    current that on September 1st Ottoman Government intends to put into effect 11
                    percent ad valorem system plus consumption taxes. Refer to Department’s 86,
                    November 15, 6 p.m.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d866-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
